This is a greedy assignment with a local-search style refinement kept simple, so it stays well inside the time limit.

**Approach.** Process vehicles by their earliest-free time using a priority queue. For the vehicle that becomes free first, scan all unassigned rides and pick the one with the best value. For a ride, compute `arrive = t + dist(pos, start)` and `startTime = max(arrive, s)`. The ride is feasible only if `startTime + d <= f`. Its value is `d + (B if arrive <= s)`, divided by the time consumed, `(startTime + d - t)`. Choosing the best ratio performs better than the raw score alone. A vehicle with no feasible ride is retired.

**Cost.** Each assignment scans up to N rides. There are at most N assignments, plus F retirements, so the total is about (N+F)·N ≈ 1.1e8 simple operations, which is fine.

**Tie-breaking and scoring.** Waiting time is already included in the time consumed. A ride whose bonus can be earned scores higher because the bonus is added to the numerator. I use the ratio `(d + bonus) / (startTime + d - t)`, compared as doubles. The time used is always at least d, which is at least 1, so there is no division by zero.

**Use of the priority queue.** Pop the vehicle with the smallest time `t`. If it finds a ride, update its position and time, then push it back. If it finds none, drop it. Vehicles whose time reaches T are also dropped, since a ride must finish by f <= T anyway.

**Output.** One line per vehicle, in the form `M` followed by the ride indices. Times use `long long`.

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main(){
    int R,C,F,N,B;
    long long T;
    scanf("%d %d %d %d %d %lld",&R,&C,&F,&N,&B,&T);
    vector<int> a(N),b(N),x(N),y(N);
    vector<long long> s(N),f(N);
    for(int i=0;i<N;i++){
        scanf("%d %d %d %d %lld %lld",&a[i],&b[i],&x[i],&y[i],&s[i],&f[i]);
    }
    vector<char> used(N,0);
    vector<vector<int>> res(F);
    vector<int> pr(F,0),pc(F,0);
    typedef pair<long long,int> P;
    priority_queue<P,vector<P>,greater<P>> pq;
    for(int i=0;i<F;i++) pq.push({0,i});
    while(!pq.empty()){
        P p=pq.top();pq.pop();
        long long t=p.first;
        int v=p.second;
        int best=-1;
        double bv=-1;
        long long bend=0;
        for(int i=0;i<N;i++){
            if(used[i]) continue;
            long long arrive=t+abs(pr[v]-a[i])+abs(pc[v]-b[i]);
            long long st=max(arrive,s[i]);
            long long d=abs(x[i]-a[i])+abs(y[i]-b[i]);
            long long en=st+d;
            if(en>f[i]) continue;
            double val=(double)(d+(arrive<=s[i]?B:0))/(double)(en-t);
            if(val>bv){
                bv=val;
                best=i;
                bend=en;
            }
        }
        if(best<0) continue;
        used[best]=1;
        res[v].push_back(best);
        pr[v]=x[best];
        pc[v]=y[best];
        if(bend<T) pq.push({bend,v});
    }
    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){
        printf("%d",(int)res[i].size());
        for(int r:res[i]) printf(" %d",r);
        printf("\n");
    }
}
```
